# SafeSwitch

An AI-powered crypto trading platform where autonomous agents practice on paper before trading with real money.

## Core Flow

1. User submits risk appetite (Low / Medium / High)
2. Discovery Agent returns suggested trading pairs (ephemeral — never stored)
3. User selects pairs → each becomes an inactive **Position** in the DB
4. User activates a Position when ready → paper trading begins
5. Confidence score builds as the agent paper trades
6. User switches to live trading when confidence is high enough
7. Position completes when profit target is hit, or user stops it
8. User can request fresh suggestions at any time (market conditions change)

## Key Design Decisions

- **Suggestions are ephemeral** — returned by the API, never stored. Market context changes, so old suggestions have no value.
- **Position is the core object** — everything meaningful (confidence, P&L, trades) lives on a Position.
- **No TradingPlan layer** — the user owns a flat list of positions. Simple, like a trading terminal.
- **Paper first, always** — a position always starts in PAPER mode. The user manually switches to LIVE.

## Data Model

```
Position
├── pair           (e.g. BTC/USDT)
├── direction      (LONG | SHORT)
├── riskAppetite   (LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH)
├── status         (INACTIVE | ACTIVE | COMPLETED | STOPPED)
├── mode           (PAPER | LIVE)
├── confidence     (0–100)
├── pnl
└── trades[]

Trade
├── positionId
├── side           (BUY | SELL)
├── price, quantity, pnl
└── mode           (PAPER | LIVE)
```

## Architecture

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | TanStack Start + TanStack Query + Tailwind v4 |
| Backend | NestJS + Prisma + PostgreSQL |
| Agent loop | BullMQ + Redis (to be added) |
| Market data | Binance API (to be added) |

## Monorepo Layout

```
safeswitch/
├── frontend/     ← TanStack Start web app
├── backend/      ← NestJS API server
├── compose.yml   ← Postgres (+ Redis later)
└── justfile      ← dev commands
```
